# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

.idea/

# Exact frontend and asset tools are reproducible from the committed manifests.
node_modules/
.tools/
dist/
.test-build/
.vite/

# Python is only a host for the deterministic Blender recipe. Import caches are
# never reviewed generator inputs or outputs.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# `lab trace` output. Regenerated from a seed in half a second, eight megabytes
# a fight, and reviewing one would be reviewing the simulation's own state.
web/fight*.json

# `lab learn-probe train` scratch. The checkpoint itself *is* committed -- it is
# fifteen kilobytes, it is what `lab trace --policy learned` needs, and retraining
# it costs forty-five minutes -- but its console log and the temporary an atomic
# write leaves behind are not artifacts.
checkpoints/*.log
checkpoints/*.partial

# Personal Claude Code settings and the local scripts they call. The project has no
# checked-in `.claude/settings.json` on purpose: a hook that kills processes is a
# preference about one machine, not a contract every contributor inherits.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/local/
